      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/AnnotationReanchorService.cs — try `paraId` resolution FIRST; fall back to the existing textPattern+Levenshtein+paragraphHint scorer as the cross-Word-session fallback (FR-11)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs — use paraId as the splice key mapping edited editor paragraphs to original OOXML paragraphs (FR-12; the mapping the FR-02 splice in task 020 consumes)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/DocxAnnotationReader.cs / DocxAnnotationWriter.cs — the annotation contract shapes that carry the anchor; keep the anchor additive so writer/reader stay compatible</file>
      <file role="reference">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/notes/spikes/ — S1/S1b (paraId preserved on unchanged paragraphs — the within-round-trip case) + S2 (client carry); the Word-regeneration caveat is the external-edit case the fuzzy fallback covers</file>
      <file role="design">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r3/design.md §5 + §5.2 (Word-regeneration caveat — paraId-primary + fuzzy fallback), §6.2 (paraId + offsets on the anchor), §2 (Current State — AnchoredAnnotationAnchor compose-contracts.ts:108-115 + AnnotationReanchorService.cs), §8 (SAVE splice-by-paraId), §10 (reuse map — re-anchor service row), §11 (ADR Tension Path A)</file>
    </relevant-files>
