  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-11 / design §5.2">Resolution order is paraId-FIRST, fuzzy-FALLBACK. `AnnotationReanchorService`'s textPattern+Levenshtein+paragraphHint matcher MUST be retained (not deleted) as the cross-Word-session fallback — Word regenerates all paraIds on external save (Open-XML-SDK #925).</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-12">On save, paraId is the key that maps each edited editor paragraph to exactly one original OOXML paragraph for the FR-02 splice. An edit to paragraph P updates exactly the original paragraph with matching paraId.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR Tension Path A (design §11 / project CLAUDE.md)">`AnchoredAnnotation` gains `paraId`/offsets but stays Compose-domain positional document-adjacent UI state — never written via `memory.*` (inherited R2 deviation). Contract change is ADDITIVE; existing fields remain.</constraint>
    <constraint source="mirror-first / project">The `paraId` field is added mirror-first: client `compose-contracts.ts` ↔ server anchor contract stay in sync. Do not fork the schema.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">No `Microsoft.Graph` types above the `SpeFileStore`/Infrastructure facade in the reanchor/splice code (`Services/Compose/`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-05">`Services/Compose/` injects no AI internals (`IOpenAiClient`/executor/routing) — Tier-1 NetArchTest stays green.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06 / ADR-038">Ships a through-the-wire `WebApplicationFactory` seam slice test (`tests/integration/seam/**`) proving an anchor round-trips to the correct paragraph by paraId. No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration/ctor-null tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029 / NFR-01 / CLAUDE.md §10">Measure BFF publish size on this BFF-touching task; report absolute compressed + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (state PDB convention); ≤60 MB; verify no new HIGH CVE. Run `/conflict-check` before the BFF PR (AnnotationReanchorService is a shared seam; parallel-safe=false).</constraint>
  </constraints>

