  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + dependency check">Confirm tasks 010 (paraId map) + 011 (client carry) are available. Read design §5.2 (Word-regeneration caveat) + §8 (splice-by-paraId) + §11 (ADR Tension Path A). Output the FULL rigor-level declaration. Load the knowledge files + `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Add the additive paraId field (mirror-first)">Add `paraId` to `AnchoredAnnotationAnchor` (`compose-contracts.ts:108-115`) and to the server anchor contract in the same shape; keep `textPattern`/`paragraphHint`/`spanId`. Document the Path A rationale (stays Compose-domain, never `memory.*`) in the PR description.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Promote paraId to primary anchor (FR-11)">In `AnnotationReanchorService.cs`, resolve by `paraId` first; when the paraId is absent (external Word edit regenerated ids), delegate to the retained textPattern+Levenshtein+paragraphHint scorer. Do NOT remove the fuzzy path.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Wire paraId as splice key (FR-12)">In `ComposeService`, establish the paraId→original-OOXML-paragraph mapping that the FR-02 splice (task 020) consumes, so an edited editor paragraph maps to exactly the original paragraph with matching paraId.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Unit tests">Assert: (a) an anchor resolves by paraId within our round-trip; (b) the SAME anchor re-resolves via the fuzzy matcher after an external edit that changed/removed the paraId; (c) an edit to paragraph P maps to exactly the original paragraph with matching paraId; (d) the anchor contract is additive (existing consumers unaffected). Real docx/round-trip; no transport mocks (ADR-038).</step>
    <step order="5" name="Through-the-wire slice test (NFR-06)">Add a `WebApplicationFactory` slice test in `tests/integration/seam/**` proving an anchor round-trips to the correct paragraph by paraId (load → anchor → save → reload).</step>
    <step order="6" name="Verify + size/CVE report">Build BFF; build the shared lib for the client contract change. Run the new tests. Report publish-size absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (PDB convention); no new HIGH CVE. NetArchTest facade + Graph-isolation green. Update TASK-INDEX status.</step>
  </steps>

