  <justification>
    <existing>`AnnotationReanchorService` already resolves anchors (textPattern+Levenshtein+paragraphHint) and `AnchoredAnnotationAnchor` already carries the anchor fields — this task EXTENDS both, it does not add a component. Verified against design §2 (Current State) + `compose-contracts.ts:108-115`.</existing>
    <extension>The `paraId` field is added to the EXISTING anchor contract and the paraId-first ordering wraps the EXISTING scorer — the fuzzy matcher is retained (required, per the Word-regeneration caveat), not replaced. No new service; the splice-key mapping lives on the existing `ComposeService` save path.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without paraId-primary anchoring + the splice-key mapping, redlines/annotations keep drifting on fuzzy text+index (the R2 stale-selection bug class, DEF-09) and the E1 delta save has no key to map edited editor paragraphs to original OOXML paragraphs. Concrete failing contract: FR-11 "an anchor resolves by paraId within our round-trip and by fuzzy match after an external Word edit" and FR-12 "an edit to paragraph P updates exactly the original paragraph with matching paraId" are unmet, blocking the FR-02 splice (task 020).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">An annotation/redline anchor resolves by `paraId` within our own load→edit→save round-trip (FR-11 acceptance).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The SAME anchor re-resolves via the retained `AnnotationReanchorService` fuzzy matcher after an external Word edit that regenerated/removed paraIds — the fuzzy path is NOT deleted (FR-11 acceptance / design §5.2).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">On save, an edit to paragraph P maps to exactly the original OOXML paragraph with the matching paraId (FR-12 acceptance) — the splice key the FR-02 rebuild consumes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`paraId` is added to `AnchoredAnnotationAnchor` as an additive field (client mirror + server contract in sync); existing `textPattern`/`paragraphHint`/`spanId` consumers are unaffected (ADR Tension Path A — stays Compose-domain, never `memory.*`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A through-the-wire `WebApplicationFactory` slice test proves an anchor round-trips to the correct paragraph by paraId (NFR-06).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`Services/Compose/` injects no AI-internal type (NetArchTest green); no `Microsoft.Graph` type leaks above the facade (ADR-007).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish size reported absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline, ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE; PDB convention stated.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Unit + slice tests exist and pass; BFF build + shared-lib build green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

